1. Definitions
   a) "Prohibited Entity" means:
      (i) Any national, state, provincial, or local government or
          any of their agencies or instrumentalities.
      (ii) Any military, law enforcement, or intelligence
           organisation.
      (iii) Any political party, political campaign, or political
            action committee.
      (iv) Any corporation or organisation majority-owned or
           controlled by any of the above.
   b) "Prohibited Purpose" means:
      (i) Development, deployment, or operation of any weapon
          or weapon system.
      (ii) Mass surveillance, tracking, or profiling of persons
           without explicit, informed consent.
      (iii) Political campaigning, propaganda, or influence
            operations.
      (iv) Any activity in violation of international criminal
           law, including war crimes, crimes against humanity,
           or genocide.
   c) "Humanitarian Use" means activities conducted solely for
      the immediate preservation of human life, provision of
      medical care, disaster relief, protection of the vulnerable,
      or restoration of essential civilian infrastructure in
      accordance with international humanitarian law.

2. Independence Requirement
